
1. Objective

=> To restrict access to an S3 bucket so that only authorized users or roles can access specific resources, ensuring data security and compliance.

2. Steps Performed

- Created an S3 bucket for storing sensitive data.
- Defined and attached a custom bucket policy to allow access only from specific IAM users, roles, or IP addresses.
- Tested access with authorized and unauthorized users to verify restrictions.
- Enabled logging and monitoring for the S3 bucket to track access attempts.

3. Security Learnings

- Restricting S3 access using bucket policies and IAM ensures only intended users can access data.
- Regularly review and update policies to maintain least privilege.
- Enable logging (e.g., S3 access logs, CloudTrail) to monitor and audit access.
- Avoid using public access unless absolutely necessary.
